# ---- MIW build rules moved out: build_intrinsic / intrinsic_split /
# ---- intrinsic_sidecar / wfs_intrinsic_sidecar / refit_mi -------------------
# Phase 3a of notes/status/organization_plan.md moved these five rules into the miw
# product, rubinwork/products/miw/Snakefile, which writes into the product data root.
# The study rules below still READ the MIW at the paths they always did --
# output/miw/<P>_<M>/{intrinsic_split_*,zk_intrinsic,fits}.parquet and
# output/miw/<P>_<M>/build/rot_<lo>_<hi>/intrinsic_grid.parquet in this old tree -- so
# those files are now INPUTS this Snakefile does not build.  Rebuild one with the product
# Snakefile, or (until phase 5 retires the old tree) leave the existing output in place.
#
# `refit_mi` went with them: its fits.parquet is a function of the MIW variant alone, and
# fam_tables already owns the plain `fit` rule that calls the same run_dz_fit.py without a
# sidecar.  So the two fits live in the two products whose configuration each belongs to.
#
# Only three of the twelve (param_set, mi_name) pairs have a COMPLETE MIW on disk, so
# MI_PAIRS above filters on what exists and reports the rest -- see the comment there.

# (rule intrinsic_split moved to rubinwork/products/miw/Snakefile -- see above)

